# Line-ending normalization.
#
# Why this file exists: four different agents (Claude, Codex, Cursor, and the
# owner's Windows editors) write into this working tree. Without normalization,
# a Windows tool rewriting CRLF endings produces diffs where every line of a
# file appears changed — on 2026-09-27 that was 307 phantom line changes across
# five files with zero content change. Phantom diffs bury real ones, and a real
# defect hidden inside 307 noise lines is how a broken service worker ships.
#
# Rule: text files are stored LF in the repository. Checkout behavior is left to
# each tool, so Windows editors keep working normally.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.wav   binary

# Windows-only helper scripts are expected to have CRLF on disk.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
